  "source": {
    "document": "WebSocket Streams for Binance — \"General WSS information\" (24-hour connection lifetime; server ping every 20s), \"Server Shutdown\", \"Trade Streams\", \"Individual Symbol Book Ticker Streams\"",
    "url": "https://github.com/binance/binance-spot-api-docs/blob/master/web-socket-streams.md#general-wss-information",
    "accessedAt": "2026-08-27"
  },
  "notes": [
    "SYNTHETIC SESSION. Frame shapes are documented; the disconnect/reconnect SCRIPT is composed here, because the venue publishes no example transcript.",
    "The venue facts it exercises: a single connection is valid for at most 24 hours and 'expect to be disconnected at the 24 hour mark'; a `serverShutdown` event precedes a shutdown and instructs establishing a new connection; and the documentation defines NO replay, resume, or backfill parameter for `<symbol>@trade` or `<symbol>@bookTicker`.",
    "Because there is no replay, a reconnect cannot claim continuity: the expected result is `FeedConnected` + `FeedGapDetected` (+ incident), and NEVER `FeedResynchronized` (ADR-002 §2.4).",
    "Elapsed times are the driver's; they are not venue facts."
  ],
